			{
				"type": "Comment",
				"start": 0,
				"end": 549,
				"data": "\n\tThe hoisted-edge trim reads the EDGE, not the neighbour's kind: `clean_nodes` lifts a\n\t`{@debug}` out of the fragment before it trims, so whatever sibling stands beside it is the\n\tfragment's first/last node and the run between them is render-free. A sibling whose own\n\tnewline flows — an inline element, a component, a tag — therefore reaches the glued form, as\n\ta text sibling already does. A sibling that owns its line keeps the run as its separator,\n\tand so does one that is itself hoisted — the fragment then has no content end at all.\n"
			},
			{
				"type": "Text",
				"start": 549,
				"end": 551,
				"raw": "\n\n",
				"data": "\n\n"
			},
